    "summary": "The dependency file is in mixed health: requests and flask are well-maintained and recommended, but two production dependencies are abandoned. The most urgent problem is pycrypto, an abandoned cryptographic library with four known vulnerabilities including a critical buffer overflow and weak key generation, followed by nose, which has had no release in over 11 years and no maintenance path. Separately, the pinned requests 2.31.0 carries 6 known vulnerabilities and the bottom of the flask range (3.0.x) carries 2, both fixed in newer releases. The single most valuable next step is replacing pycrypto with a maintained alternative such as pycryptodome or cryptography.",
